{"type":"standard","title":"Welsh language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Welsh language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q9309","titles":{"canonical":"Welsh_language","normalized":"Welsh language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Welsh language</span></span>"},"pageid":33545,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Welsh_speakers_in_the_2021_census.svg/330px-Welsh_speakers_in_the_2021_census.svg.png","width":330,"height":362},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Welsh_speakers_in_the_2021_census.svg/960px-Welsh_speakers_in_the_2021_census.svg.png","width":512,"height":561},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1355141740","tid":"22c07822-53ff-11f1-bc2d-60714e77601c","timestamp":"2026-05-20T03:51:09Z","description":"Brittonic language","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Welsh_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Welsh_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Welsh_language"}},"extract":"Welsh is a Celtic language of the Brittonic subgroup that is native to the Welsh people. Welsh is spoken natively in Wales by about 18% of the population, by some in England, and in Y Wladfa. Historically, it has also been known in English as British, Cambrian, Cambric and Cymric.","extract_html":"<p><b>Welsh</b> is a Celtic language of the Brittonic subgroup that is native to the Welsh people. Welsh is spoken natively in Wales by about 18% of the population, by some in England, and in <span><span style=\"font-style:normal\">Y Wladfa</span></span>. Historically, it has also been known in English as <b>British</b>, <b>Cambrian</b>, <b>Cambric</b> and <b>Cymric</b>.</p>"}